 # 21\. Preference Matching Logic

 Create a simple recommendation algorithm.

 For example:

 Each destination has tags:

```
{
  activities: ["hiking", "nature", "photography"],
  styles: ["adventure", "solo"],
  environments: ["mountains"],
  budget: "comfortable",
  pace: "balanced"
}
```

 Compare the user's preferences against destination attributes.

 Calculate a match score from 0-100.

 Example:

```
Activities match: 30%
Travel style: 20%
Destination type: 20%
Budget: 15%
Travel pace: 10%
Season: 5%
```

 Use the resulting score to sort destinations.

 Show:

 "92% Match"

 instead of simply showing random recommendations.

 Keep this logic modular so it can later be replaced with an AI recommendation system.

